    "title": "## Architecture",
    "text": "A markdown document in the corpus can reference another node (an artifact, a folder, a heading, a block) both before it has ever been ingested into Apeiron and after. The two addressing styles this implies aren't two permanent, freely-interchangeable choices — they map to a lifecycle (see [discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TG001)):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8003",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8004",
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D59000B",
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D59000C"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8003:props:StringProp:00CE59A358000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8003:props:StringProp:00CE59A358001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Slugified-path addressing**",
    "text": "**Slugified-path addressing**: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8003' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> a path of `slugify()`-derived segments, computable directly from the raw markdown text itself. This is deliberately manual, and the only option before ingestion: a writer hand-injects it while authoring or refactoring a doc, before any node id exists to reference instead.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Node-ID addressing**",
    "text": "**Node-ID addressing**: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8004' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> a stable, opaque identifier (a snowflake, minted once at node creation, never derived from or invalidated by content) that only exists *after* ingestion.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007:links:Link:00CDBZ7C5G000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBZ76TG002",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007:links:Link:00CDBZ7C5G000:props:StringProp:00CDBZ7C5G001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "287"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "## Topology",
    "text": "The canonical stored form for any internal reference is a standard CommonMark link, `[title](target)`. No separate bracket syntax (`[[link]]`) is needed for this, at least for now — the syntactic markers below already make an internal reference unambiguous without an extra wrapper (see [discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TG002)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8008",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8009",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800C",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG005",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00E",
    "text": "Two syntactic contexts apply orthogonally to the two addressing styles from Architecture.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### In-App Context",
    "text": "Resolved directly against the graph by Apeiron's own tooling (`kg:tree`, `kg:unfold`, a future webapp), never against files on disk. Canonical syntax uses the `aperas://` scheme:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800A",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800A:props:StringProp:00CE59A118000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800A:props:StringProp:00CE59A118001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "`[title](aperas://tree/<block-slug-path>)`",
    "text": "`[title](aperas://tree/<block-slug-path>)`: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800A' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> slugified-path addressing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`[title](aperas://id/<ID>)`",
    "text": "`[title](aperas://id/<ID>)`: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800B' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> node-ID addressing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Projected/Pre-Ingestion Context",
    "text": "A markdown file meant to also work as a plain file on disk (a projected artifact, or a doc being authored/refactored before ingestion). Compatible syntax uses an ordinary relative file link with a `#fragment`:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800D",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800E",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800F",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800D:props:StringProp:00CE599Z7G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800D:props:StringProp:00CE599Z7G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "`[title](../folder/file#<block-slug-path>)`",
    "text": "`[title](../folder/file#<block-slug-path>)`: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800D' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> slugified-path addressing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800E:links:Link:00CDBYV548000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800E:links:Link:00CDBYV548000:props:StringProp:00CDC0D8E8000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "287"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "`[title](../folder/file#id/<ID>)`",
    "text": "`[title](../folder/file#id/<ID>)`: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800E' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> node-ID addressing, the literal `id/` fragment prefix distinguishing it from a slug-path fragment; backed by a `name=\"id/<ID>\"` anchor, same mechanism as the slug-path form (see [Anchors](#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00N",
    "text": "`<ID>` is always the full `Kind:snowflake` form (e.g. `BlockNode:00C5H15NT0000`), never a bare snowflake alone.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00P",
    "text": "The trailing address — `<block-slug-path>` or `id/<ID>` — is identical in both contexts; only the leading part differs (`aperas://tree/` / `aperas://id/` vs. a relative file path followed by `#`). Translating a reference between the two contexts is therefore only ever a leading-part swap, never a change to the trailing address itself.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H:links:Link:00CDBZ7C68000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBZ76TG004",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H:links:Link:00CDBZ7C68000:props:StringProp:00CDBZ7C68001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "469"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Anchors",
    "text": "A target block carries its anchor(s) inline, tagged with a `class` identifying which kind — never as a separate preceding line. `<a>` isn't a CommonMark block-level HTML tag, so a standalone `<a name=...></a>` line doesn't stay structurally inert: it parses as an ordinary paragraph and gets consumed as the following heading's own leading text, reordering it on projection and, where real leading prose already exists, displacing that prose into a separate block (see [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TG004)). Placement is block-shape-specific:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800J",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800K",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800M",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800N",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800P",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800Q",
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D59000Y",
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D590011"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00R",
    "text": "**Heading** — appended to the end of the heading's own line. Before ingestion:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00S",
    "text": "```markdown\n### Sub 1.1 <a name='--top-heading/---sub-1/----sub-1-1' class='aperas-anchor aperas-tree'></a>\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00T",
    "text": "After ingestion, once a node id exists, the id anchor is added alongside:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00V",
    "text": "```markdown\n### Sub 1.1 <a name='--top-heading/---sub-1/----sub-1-1' class='aperas-anchor aperas-tree'></a><a name='id/BlockNode:00C5H15NT0000' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a>\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00W",
    "text": "**List item / paragraph** — inline, right after the lead-in colon:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR00X",
    "text": "```markdown\n- **Term**: <a name='id/BlockNode:00C5H15NT0000' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> rest of text\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000:links:Link:00CDBZ7C80000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800A",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000:links:Link:00CDBZ7C80000:props:StringProp:00CDBZ7C80001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "124"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Lead-In Term Detection",
    "text": "A list item or paragraph's lead-in term (the colon-delimited title an unbounded-depth list uses in place of a heading — see [Issues](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800A)) is found by walking the block's own parsed inline structure, not by scanning raw characters: a candidate colon (`:`, or `：` for Japanese) is only accepted if it sits in plain visible text — never inside inline code (`` `Kind:snowflake` ``'s own colon is data, not punctuation) and never inside a `**bold**`/`*italic*` span. A rejected candidate doesn't end the search; scanning continues for a later one in the same text.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D590013",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAXR016",
    "text": "Which script's rules apply is read from a `lang: en|ja|vi` frontmatter field (English, Japanese, Vietnamese — the first three supported), defaulting to `en`. Vietnamese, like English, is space-delimited and uses the word-count cap; only Japanese uses the character-count cap and skips the space-after-colon check (Japanese prose isn't space-delimited at all).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG005:links:Link:00CDBZ7C8R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBZ76TG006",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG005:links:Link:00CDBZ7C8R000:props:StringProp:00CDBZ7C90000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "678"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Anchor-Matching Requirement for Resolution",
    "text": "Finding a name-token or id match for a reference's target (the existing deep-path walk, or a direct id lookup) only produces a *candidate* — it's accepted as the actual resolution target only if that candidate also carries a `class=\"aperas-anchor\"` tag whose `name` equals the fragment being resolved (the heading's stashed anchor, or a literal scan of a list item's/paragraph's own `text`). A block nobody tagged is never mistaken for a link target this way, which is what disambiguates an internal reference from an ordinary, unrelated same-page anchor link (e.g. `[jump to top](#top)`) now that there's no `[[...]]`-style wrapper marking intent the way there was before (see [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TG006)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Full-Path Collisions",
    "text": "Two blocks must never resolve to the same full `<block-slug-path>` — a hard authoring error (reject at write time: ingestion, `kg:insert`, or `kg:update`), not a case needing disambiguation. Reusing the same heading *title* at different tree positions is ordinary (e.g. two sibling sections each with their own \"Overview\" subheading) and never collides, since their full paths differ by their distinct ancestor segments; only two blocks at the exact same tree position with the exact same heading text would produce an identical full path, which is a genuine duplicate.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG007:links:Link:00CDBYV570000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG007:links:Link:00CDBYV570000:props:StringProp:00CDBYV570001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "333"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "## Workflows",
    "text": "Authoring a cross-reference before ingestion: compute the target's slug path and write it as a standard link with a `#fragment`, backed by a hand-written `<a name=\"...\" class=\"aperas-anchor aperas-tree\">` anchor placed inline on the target's own line — appended to the heading's line, or right after a list item's lead-in colon (see [Anchors](#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800H)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D598006",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG009",
      "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG00A",
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D598009"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAY0001",
    "text": "Authoring a cross-reference after ingestion, where the target already has a node id: address it directly with the `id/<ID>` (or `aperas://id/<ID>`) form.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RAY0002",
    "text": "Once every referrer has itself been ingested and so no longer needs the compatibility form, a cleanup pass removes the block's `aperas-tree` anchor, leaving only `aperas-id`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
