          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Cross-artifact link staleness on ingestion**",
    "text": "**Cross-artifact link staleness on ingestion**: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800H' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> resolved — an artifact whose own text doesn't change is never re-ingested on its own, so a link it couldn't resolve stayed stale even after its target came into existence elsewhere in the corpus, with no way to fix it short of hand-editing `ingestedHash` to force a re-ingest. `kg:ingest` now stashes every code a block fails to resolve on its own referring artifact, and retries every stashed code against the current graph after its main work is done, force-reingesting (without discarding reconciliation identity — see [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TR008) for the `hadContent`/`bypassUnchangedCheck` distinction) any artifact where at least one now resolves. See [Workflows](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG007).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
