    ],
    "title": "00CDC0RCCR008",
    "text": "**A lead-in colon followed only by nested list children got no title**: resolved — `findLeadInColonOffset`'s space-after-colon check read the next character from the colon's own mdast text node, which simply ends at the colon when nothing inline follows it on the same line (e.g. `- **Heading**:` before a nested list), and treated that the same as a genuinely ambiguous no-space case. Fixed by accepting \"nothing left in this text run\" the same as \"a space follows\" — the inline-code and bold/italic exclusions run first and are unaffected. See [Lead-In Term Detection](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000) and [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TR00E).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800K:links:Link:00CDBYV5P0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG005",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
