    ],
    "title": "**Discussion**",
    "text": "**Discussion**: [Motivation — the mixing problem](../discussion/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002) — rationale for adopting block-based separation, evidenced by the pre-Phase-1.1 corpus.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80005:links:Link:00CDDBQ9G0002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0004",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80005:links:Link:00CDDBQ9G0002:props:StringProp:00CDDBQ9G8000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Issues**",
    "text": "**Issues**: [Resolved: Context/Discussion boundary](../issues/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CDD68FE0004) — Context conflicted with Discussion's \"motivation\"; resolved by defining Context as a factual index, not narrative.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**History**",
    "text": "**History**: to be updated.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Architecture",
    "text": "To achieve pure Perata (clean projections for the reader), the storage layer must adopt a **Block-Based Separation of Concerns**. Instead of one mixed file, the Apeiron stores strictly isolated documents (or trees):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E80008",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E80009",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000A",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000B",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000C",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80008:props:StringProp:00CE5999C0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80008:props:StringProp:00CE5999C0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR008",
    "text": "**Design Docs:** Pure architectural specifications, data models, and rules.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR009",
    "text": "**Issue Docs:** Bug reports, architectural gaps, and pending fixes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00A",
    "text": "**Planning Docs:** Implementation plans, task breakdowns, and step-by-step execution guides.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00B",
    "text": "**History/Status Docs:** What was implemented, when it was verified, and milestones.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00C",
    "text": "**Discussion Docs:** Rejected ideas, motivation, and theoretical context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00D",
    "text": "This guarantees that a reader parsing the \"Design Doc\" sees *only* the design, without needing complex transducers to strip out bug reports and history logs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Topology",
    "text": "A rigid physical directory structure inevitably fails because software development requires different lenses at different times (e.g., building a feature vs. fixing a cross-cutting bug). Because all edits happen on the unbounded tree (Apeiron), we optimize physical storage for the **Reader** (stability) and use TreeViews/Freeflow documents for the **Agent** (dynamic tasks).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000F",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Physical Storage: Concern-Centric",
    "text": "At the file-system layer, artifacts are strictly grouped by concern. This forms the system-wide documentation naturally.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00G",
    "text": "```text\nartifacts/\n  ├── design/\n  │   ├── crud.md                 (Pure Perata: Architecture, Models, Specs)\n  │   └── treeview.md\n  ├── issues/\n  │   ├── crud.md                 (Bugs, gaps, pending tasks)\n  │   └── network.md\n  ├── planning/\n  │   └── crud.md                 (Implementation plans, step-by-step execution guides)\n  ├── history/\n  │   └── crud.md                 (Implementation status, log of changes)\n  └── discussion/\n      └── crud.md                 (Rationale, rejected ideas, unstructured thought)\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000F",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Document-Level Skeletons",
    "text": "To ensure uniformity across the corpus, each concern document should follow a strict top-level heading structure. Standardizing these paths (e.g., `design/crud.md/Data-Model`) allows the agent to reliably address them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000J",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000N",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000Q",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000J:props:StringProp:00CE5997TG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000J:props:StringProp:00CE5997TG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Design Docs (`design/*.md`)**",
    "text": "**Design Docs (`design/*.md`)**: Only normative, current-state architectural facts. No \"I think we should...\"",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000K",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000M"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000K:props:StringProp:00CE5996K0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000K:props:StringProp:00CE5996K0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00K",
    "text": "`# Context` — a factual index of this concern's discussion, issue, planning, and history docs: one link plus a brief, non-argumentative summary per doc (what exists, not why). Rationale, rejected alternatives, and narrative stay in the linked Discussion doc — never inline here.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00M",
    "text": "`# Architecture`, `# Topology`, `# Workflows`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Issue Docs (`issues/*.md`)**",
    "text": "**Issue Docs (`issues/*.md`)**: Actionable, resolvable nodes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000P"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000P:props:StringProp:00CE5995GR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000P:props:StringProp:00CE5995GR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00P",
    "text": "`# Open Issues`, `# Pending Tasks`, `# Resolved`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Planning Docs (`planning/*.md`)**",
    "text": "**Planning Docs (`planning/*.md`)**: Actionable steps and plans for implementation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000R"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000R:props:StringProp:00CE5993SG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000R:props:StringProp:00CE5993SG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00R",
    "text": "`# Implementation Plan`, `# Task Breakdown`, `# Verification Plan`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**History Docs (`history/*.md`)**",
    "text": "**History Docs (`history/*.md`)**: Chronological or state-based facts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88001:props:StringProp:00CE59930R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88001:props:StringProp:00CE599310000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00T",
    "text": "`# Current Status`, `# Milestones`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Workflows",
    "text": "The strict physical isolation of concerns is necessary for long-term health, but it is hostile to the creative process. The Aperas workflow bridges this gap by using a **Freeflow Artifact** in the `discussion/` directory as the active workspace.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88003",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88008",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800B",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00W",
    "text": "When starting a task, the agent doesn't jump between `design.md` and `issues.md`. They create a freeflow discussion document, which serves two simultaneous purposes:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### The Dashboard (Context Assembly)",
    "text": "The top of the freeflow document acts as a control panel. The agent authors structural links to all the formal blocks across the corpus that are relevant to the current task.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88005",
      "BlockNode:00CDF7V7VR00Z",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR00Y",
    "text": "**`discussion/crud-reconciliation-task.md`**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR010",
    "text": "*(By linking these, the agent anchors the formal state into their workspace. When unfolded via `TreeView`, it projects all these scattered formal blocks into a single localized lens).*",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### The Scratchpad (Freeflow Authoring)",
    "text": "Beneath the dashboard, the agent dumps unstructured, messy thoughts exactly as they do today.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88009",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800A",
      "BlockNode:00CE9FTDAR004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CE9FTDAR002",
    "text": "```markdown\n## Brainstorming\nSo the issue happens because the parent node is missing.\nIf we use a placeholder flag on the node, it could reconcile safely...\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88008",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CE9FTDAR003",
    "text": "This is pure Apeiron. It is unbounded, unstructured, and safe from strict schema rules. It exists only in the discussion concern.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Crystallization (The Update Loop)",
    "text": "Eventually, the brainstorming yields a concrete decision. The thought *crystallizes* from a messy idea into a formal architectural rule, or a formal task.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDF7V7VR015",
      "BlockNode:00CDF7V7VR016"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### The Resulting Ecosystem",
    "text": "This creates a perfect symbiosis:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800F",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800G",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800F:props:StringProp:00CE59925R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800F:props:StringProp:00CE59925R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDF7V7VR018",
    "text": "The **Freeflow Document** (in `discussion/`) retains the entire historical journey of the thought process, the rejected ideas, and the dashboard of links that defined the task context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7W0000",
    "text": "The **Formal Documents** (in `design/`, `issues/`, `planning/`, `history/`) remain pristine and strictly isolated, containing only the crystallized reality of the system.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDF7V7W0001",
    "text": "The **Agent** navigates the graph easily, using the freeflow document as a central hub that fans out to the formal specs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Documentation Architecture — Discussion",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CDD68DSG000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Motivation: The Mixing Problem",
    "text": "Currently, documents in `AperasKG/artifacts/` are massive mixtures of completely different logical concerns. Looking at actual project files (e.g., `Aperas-crud-design.md` and `Aperas-treeview-design.md`), the writer often mixes everything into a single document and sometimes even the same paragraph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
      "BlockNode:00CDDBVXAR002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAG003",
    "text": "No transducer or adapter can automatically untangle this. A single artifact today contains:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8004",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8005",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8006",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8007",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8008"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8004:props:StringProp:00CE5990QR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8004:props:StringProp:00CE5990QR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDDBVXAG004",
    "text": "**Core Design:** The actual specification (e.g., `3. Core model: placeholder is a flag`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAG005",
    "text": "**Issues & Gaps:** Bugs discovered live during implementation (e.g., `6. Bookkeeping gaps found while designing this`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAG006",
    "text": "**History & Status:** Implementation progress and verification records (e.g., `Status: implemented, live-verified against a synthetic graph`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAR000",
    "text": "**Discussion & Rationale:** Why something was built a certain way, or rejected (e.g., `12. Considered and rejected`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAR001",
    "text": "**Implementation Details:** Notes to self about code structure.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Documentation — Issues",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CDD68DSG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0002",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0003",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0004"
    ]
  },
  {
