    "text": "`spawnService()` hardcoded spawning `tsx` + a separate `service.ts` file — which doesn't exist once bundled (`service.ts`'s code is inlined into the one `aperas.js`, no file of its own anymore). Fixed: `service.ts` now exports its own `main`; `aperas.ts` recognizes a hidden `--__service` verb (checked before normal dispatch) that dynamically imports and runs it — the dynamic import is also what makes `esbuild` include `service.ts`'s code in the bundle at all, since nothing else reachable from `aperas.ts` ever imported it; `spawnService()` now detects dev-vs-built (does `service.ts` still exist as a sibling file?) and either spawns `tsx service.ts` (dev, unchanged) or re-invokes the running bundle itself with plain `node` + `--__service` (built).",
