      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDWQ0V88002:props:StringProp:00CE59A980001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDWQ0V88002",
    "text": "Each command's own `--help` usage line (and its missing-required-arg fallback) now prints `aperas <verb>` instead of `kg:X --` — rewritten across all 18 `kgX.ts` files.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVC8N0007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDWQ0V88003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`aperas` builds to a real `bin`",
    "text": "`aperas` builds to a real `bin`: `packages/cli/build.mjs` (`esbuild`, `oxigraph` external) produces a self-contained `packages/cli/dist/` (bundle + minimal `package.json` with a `bin` entry). Verified running standalone via plain `node`, no `tsx`, against the real graph — see [discussion](../discussion/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDWP69B8001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVC8N0007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX5H5MG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX5H5MG002:props:StringProp:00CE598G90000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX5H5MG002:props:StringProp:00CE598G90001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDX5H5MG002",
    "text": "`aperas service start` (new — today's `kg:service` only has `restart`) is the *only* place that ever reads `process.cwd()` for this. It resolves the graph (`aperas.config.json` discovery, or the dev fallback) and binds the spawned service to it, permanently, for that process's life.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDWPCC3G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX5H5MG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDX5H5MG003",
    "text": "Every other command never touches cwd for this at all. It looks for the currently running service at one fixed, well-known location — not derived from cwd, and not derived from where the code itself is installed (which also sidesteps the dev-vs-built hop-counting fragility fixed above entirely, as a side benefit: a fixed location doesn't care where the code physically sits). If nothing's there, it errors (\"no service running — run `aperas service start`\") instead of silently auto-spawning one bound to whatever cwd it happened to be called from.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDWPCC3G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX5H5MG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDX5H5MG004",
    "text": "`aperas service restart` becomes \"stop whatever's running, and re-resolve+rebind from wherever *this* invocation's cwd is\" — still explicit, still a deliberate human action.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDWPCC3G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX5H5MG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Deliberately no concurrency",
    "text": "Deliberately no concurrency: one active graph system-wide at a time, not one service per graph root. Working in two different graphs at once means explicitly restarting the service when switching, not two processes running side by side. Confirmed as the actual intent, not a limitation being settled for.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDWPCC3G001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX7VWY0002",
