    "title": "Ship the explicit-start service redesign",
    "text": "**Done.** Shipped the explicit-start service redesign: dropped auto-spawn from `ensureServiceRunning()` (errors, pointing at `aperas service start`); added `aperas service start` (binds a fresh service to the graph resolved from that invocation's own cwd) and updated `restart` to re-resolve+rebind the same way; moved the lock/socket to a fixed `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`-based location, independent of cwd and code install path. Verified live in dev and built-bundle modes, full `npm run verify` suite still clean — see [Resolved](../discussion/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R001). The one gap this pass left (client-side `getArtifactsDir()` callers not honoring the bound graph root) was closed in a follow-up pass — see [Resolved: two-path graph config](../discussion/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVCDW8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX7VWY8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX7VWY8000:links:Link:00CDY8ZXQR002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDDVCKCG002",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDX7VWY8000:links:Link:00CDY8ZXQR002:props:StringProp:00CDZVRH3G000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "412"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "Add `kg:show <ref>` (`aperas show <ref>`)",
    "text": "**Done — this Task Breakdown is complete, no open gaps.** `kg:show <ref>` (previously tracked here) turned out to be a TreeView/node-rendering gap rather than a packaging one, and moved to `AperasKG/artifacts/archive/Aperas-treeview-design.md` §16, to be picked up when that document itself gets migrated. The client-side `getArtifactsDir()` graph-root gap flagged during item 19 has since been closed too — see [history](../history/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDDVCKCG002) for the closing summary.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVCDW8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Resolved: the explicit-start service redesign, shipped and verified",
    "text": "`ensureServiceRunning()` no longer auto-spawns — it just pings, and throws `No ApeironNgn service running. Start one with: aperas service start` if nothing answers. `kgService.ts` gained `aperas service start` (binds a freshly-spawned service to the graph resolved from *this* invocation's own `process.cwd()`, or reports the existing binding if one's already running) alongside the existing `restart` (now also re-resolving and rebinding, not just restarting the process). `serviceLock.ts`'s `getRunDir()` dropped the dev-vs-built hop-counting entirely in favor of a fixed location: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/aperas`, falling back to a uid-namespaced `tmpdir()` path when unset — exactly the kind of ephemeral, per-session state `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` exists for, and the same pattern `identity.json` already established for `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`.",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CDDTBQWG000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R002",
      "BlockNode:00CDXFWK40000",
      "BlockNode:00CDXFWK40001",
      "BlockNode:00CDY3GA70002",
      "BlockNode:00CDY3GA70001",
      "BlockNode:00CDXFWK40002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R002:props:StringProp:00CE598FZG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R002:props:StringProp:00CE598FZR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDXFWK3R002",
    "text": "`graphConfig.ts` gained `resolveEffectiveGraphRoot(startDir?)` — `aperas.config.json` discovery if found, else the fixed dev fallback (now computed in one place, not duplicated across `artifacts.ts`/`store.ts`). `getArtifactsDir()`/`getApeironExportDir()` both take an optional explicit `graphRoot` now: a standalone dev tool (`verify.ts`, `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts`) omits it and keeps the old cwd-or-fallback default; `apeironNgn/service.ts` passes the graph root it was actually bound to (via `APERAS_GRAPH_ROOT`, set in the spawned child's environment by `serviceClient.ts#spawnService` — not the child's own `process.cwd()`, which is set to a fixed directory for unrelated reasons and would otherwise silently disagree with what `start` resolved).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK40000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The service's own `dehydrateToJsonLd`/`dehydrateStateToJsonLd` calls (all 4 call sites",
    "text": "The service's own `dehydrateToJsonLd`/`dehydrateStateToJsonLd` calls (all 4 call sites: `flushIfDirty`, `flushStateIfDirty`, `clobberFlush`) now pass their bound `contentDir`/`stateDir` explicitly too, instead of each defaulting to a fresh (and, before this fix, potentially divergent) resolution of its own — otherwise the \"one binding for the whole process lifetime\" guarantee would only have covered the *read* path (`rehydrateStore`), not the *write* path.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK40001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Verified live, both ways",
    "text": "Verified live, both ways: (1) dev mode — `aperas service start` binds and reports the graph root, a second `start` reports \"already running\", `restart` stops+rebinds, killing the service and running any ordinary command reports the new error instead of silently spawning one, the full `npm run verify` suite (18 checks) still passes clean; (2) built mode — a fresh `esbuild` bundle cold-started via `node packages/cli/dist/aperas.js service start` (no `tsx` anywhere) binds correctly and answers a real `tree` read.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK40002",
