    ],
    "title": "**A gap flagged, not fixed, in this pass**",
    "text": "**A gap flagged, not fixed, in this pass** (corrected below — the original write-up here was itself imprecise about where the gap actually lives): `getApeironExportDir()` got its explicit `graphRoot` argument threaded through in this pass, but `getArtifactsDir()` didn't — every caller (`apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`/`folders.ts`/`node.ts`'s `trackAllArtifacts`/`trackArtifactsScoped`/`ingestFolderTree`/`ArtifactNode.trackFromDisk`, plus `kgProject.ts`'s own `runProject`) still calls it with no argument. Those calls execute **inside the service process itself** — `service.ts`'s `handle()` invokes `runTrack`/`runIngest`/`runProject` directly on each RPC request, not the short-lived CLI client — so the resolution that runs is the *service's own* `process.cwd()`, fixed by `spawnService()` to wherever the code is installed, never the graph root `aperas service start` actually resolved and bound. Harmless today only because this repo's one `aperas.config.json` sits where the service's own cwd never reaches by walking up, so it always falls through to the cwd-independent fallback either way — a coincidence of this repo's layout, not a property of the fix. See [Resolved](../discussion/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001) below for the actual fix.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
