  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7PGG0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Workflow",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVBXH8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R001",
      "BlockNode:00CDY7T620002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDY7T61R001",
    "text": "The shared ApeironNgn service holds exactly one graph for its whole lifetime, chosen once and deliberately rather than inherited from whichever command happens to run first:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDY7PGG0001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R002",
      "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R003",
      "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R004",
      "BlockNode:00CDY7T620000",
      "BlockNode:00CDY7T620001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R002:links:Link:00CDY7T70R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDHSJQE8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R002:links:Link:00CDY7T70R000:props:StringProp:00CDZMJ1R0000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "198"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R002:props:StringProp:00CE598P5G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R002:props:StringProp:00CE598P5R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDY7T61R002",
    "text": "`aperas service start` is the only command that ever reads `process.cwd()`. It resolves the graph's Apeiron root and artifacts root from there (`aperas.config.json` discovery, or the fallback — see [Configuration](#id/BlockNode:00CDHSJQE8001)), sets both as environment variables on a freshly-spawned service, and binds it for that process's life; already running, it reports the existing binding instead of starting a second one.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDY7T61R003",
    "text": "Every other command connects to whatever's already running, at a fixed location (`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/aperas`, falling back to a uid-namespaced path under the OS temp directory when unset) — never derived from cwd or from where the code itself is installed. Nothing running? It errors (\"no service running — run `aperas service start`\") rather than silently starting one bound to an accidental cwd.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDY7T61R004",
    "text": "`aperas service stop` gracefully stops whatever's running (same SIGTERM-and-wait as the first half of `restart` below) without starting a replacement — the explicit counterpart to finding its pid and killing it by hand.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T620000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDY7T620000",
    "text": "`aperas service restart` stops whatever's running and re-resolves + rebinds from wherever *that* invocation's own cwd is — the only way to both pick up a source-code change and move the service to a different graph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDY7T620001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Deliberately no concurrency",
    "text": "Deliberately no concurrency: one active graph system-wide at a time. Working across two graphs means explicitly restarting when switching, never two service processes side by side.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDY7T61R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
