    "title": "`aperas.config.json`",
    "text": "`aperas.config.json`: created at `AperasKG/aperas.config.json` (`{ \"graph\": \".\" }`), marking `AperasKG` as its own graph root; the design doc's [Configuration](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDHSJQE8001) and [Workflow](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDY7PGG0001) sections written up to match. Verified live: stopped the service, cold-started the built bundle from a cwd deep inside `AperasKG/artifacts/`, confirmed it discovered the config by walking up (not the dev fallback) and bound to the real path; an ordinary command run from an unrelated cwd (`monorepo/`) still connected correctly through the fixed-location socket.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVCKCG003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Resolved: two-path graph config + env-var default resolution closes the artifacts-dir gap",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CDDTBQWG000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDZM8GP8001",
      "BlockNode:00CDZM8GP8002",
      "BlockNode:00CDZM8GP8003",
      "BlockNode:00CDZM8GP8004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZM8GP8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`aperas.config.json`'s `graph` field now accepts two shapes",
    "text": "`aperas.config.json`'s `graph` field now accepts two shapes: a plain string (shorthand — both `<root>/Apeiron` and `<root>/artifacts` co-located, exactly today's behavior, unchanged) or `{ \"apeiron\": \"<path>\", \"artifacts\": \"<path>\" }` (two independently-specifiable roots, for a graph whose data and markdown tree aren't co-located). `resolveGraphConfig()` resolves both forms into one `GraphConfig { apeironRoot, artifactsRoot, parent, configPath }`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZM8GP8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDZM8GP8002",
    "text": "`graphConfig.ts` gained `resolveEffectiveApeironRoot(startDir?)`/`resolveEffectiveArtifactsRoot(startDir?)`, replacing the single `resolveEffectiveGraphRoot()`. Each checks its own env var first (`APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT`/`APERAS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT`), then `aperas.config.json` discovery, then the fixed dev fallback. `getApeironExportDir()`/`getArtifactsDir()`'s own default parameters call these — unchanged call sites everywhere else, since the env-var check now lives inside the shared default resolution itself rather than being each caller's job.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZM8GP8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDZM8GP8003",
    "text": "`aperas service start`/`restart` (`kgService.ts`) resolve both roots once, from that one invocation's own cwd — still the only place cwd is read — and `spawnService()` sets both env vars on the child. Every function that calls `getArtifactsDir()`/`getApeironExportDir()` with no argument (`runTrack`, `runIngest`, `runProject`, and the shared `apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`/`folders.ts`/`node.ts` helpers) now resolves correctly with **zero signature or call-site changes**, because they're all running inside the one process that already has both env vars set for its whole lifetime — the same guarantee the \"no concurrency, one bound graph per process\" design already committed to.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZM8GP8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDZM8GP8004",
    "text": "This replaces the parameter-threading approach the gap note above originally assumed was necessary: threading an explicit root through `runTrack`/`runIngest`/`runProject` and every function they call would have meant touching upwards of a dozen call sites across `apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`, `folders.ts`, `node.ts`, plus every one of `verify.ts`'s direct calls into them. The env-var default achieves the same correctness for free, because the architecture already guarantees a service process is bound to exactly one graph for its entire life — parameter-threading would only earn its keep if a single process needed to serve different graphs per call, which this design deliberately never does.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZQJVG8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZQJVG8002:links:Link:00CDZQJWR8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZQJVG8002:links:Link:00CDZQJWR8000:props:StringProp:00CDZQJWR8001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "920"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZQJVG8002:props:StringProp:00CE59A75G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDZQJVG8002:props:StringProp:00CE59A75G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Closed the client-side graph-root gap",
    "text": "Closed the client-side graph-root gap: `aperas.config.json`'s `graph` field now takes either a plain path (shorthand) or `{ \"apeiron\": \"...\", \"artifacts\": \"...\" }` (independent roots); `resolveEffectiveApeironRoot()`/`resolveEffectiveArtifactsRoot()` (`graphConfig.ts`) each check their own env var (`APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT`/`APERAS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT`, set by `aperas service start`/`restart`) before config discovery/the fallback. `getArtifactsDir()`'s existing callers — `runTrack`/`runIngest`/`runProject` and the shared `apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`/`folders.ts`/`node.ts` helpers — needed no signature changes at all. Verified live: cold-started the built bundle from a cwd deep inside `AperasKG/`, confirmed the lock recorded the real (non-fallback) discovered paths for both roots, then ran `aperas project` from an unrelated cwd (`monorepo/`) and confirmed it read and wrote against the correctly-bound `artifacts/` — see [discussion](../discussion/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDZM30JG001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVC8N0007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
