    ],
    "title": "Two-path graph config, gap closed",
    "text": "Two-path graph config, gap closed: `aperas.config.json`'s `graph` field now takes either a plain path (shorthand) or `{ \"apeiron\": \"...\", \"artifacts\": \"...\" }` (independent roots). `getArtifactsDir()`'s remaining callers (`runTrack`/`runIngest`/`runProject`, the shared `apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`/`folders.ts`/`node.ts` helpers) now resolve correctly via an env-var-first default (`APERAS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT`, set alongside `APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT` at `aperas service start`/`restart` time), with zero signature changes anywhere. Verified live: cold-started the built bundle from a cwd deep inside `AperasKG/`, confirmed the lock recorded the real discovered paths for both roots (not the coincidental fallback), then ran `aperas project` from an unrelated cwd and confirmed it read/wrote against the correctly-bound `artifacts/`. Closes the one gap flagged in the previous milestone.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVCKCG003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
