  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE01Y42R00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-11T07:38:05.725Z",
    "title": "## Freeflow: why newest-first",
    "text": "The ApeironNgn-era docs describe the substrate this migration itself runs on (`store.ts`, `artifacts.ts`, reconciliation, addressing) — getting that into the graph early means later sub-tasks (including the TDB-era ones, which are pure history at this point) can link back to live design docs instead of archived prose. TDB-era docs don't block anything downstream, so they go last.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE01Y42R001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE01Y42R00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-11T07:09:06.091Z",
    "title": "## Freeflow: open question — is `tdb-era/` even a design/issues/planning/history split?",
    "text": "Everything in `tdb-era/` describes a retired substrate. Design docs are supposed to be \"current-state architectural facts,\" but none of that architecture is current anymore. Leaning toward treating it more like a history-heavy concern doc set (maybe skipping `issues`/`planning` entirely, since there's nothing left to plan or fix) — not settled; revisit when that sub-task actually starts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE01Y42R001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
