    "title": "For `tdb-era/` specifically",
    "text": "For `tdb-era/` specifically (this includes `Aperas-dev-status.md`, which is TDB-era in origin despite sitting at the `archive/` top level — pulled out only because its coverage spans many future dev phases too broad for that folder): don't decompose the old docs 1:1. Instead, for whatever knowledge in them is still live in the current (ApeironNgn) system, author brand-new concern docs reflecting today's understanding — following Document Topology from the start, with concern names chosen up front to avoid any collision (no post-hoc rename needed, unlike the `cli.md` → `packaging.md` incident). Anything no longer live goes to that concern's `history` doc as retired background, not carried into `design`. See [Settled](../discussion/archive-migration.md#id/BlockNode:00CE0HD0HG002).",
