    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58006:props:StringProp:00CE598MH8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58006:props:StringProp:00CE598MH8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CE1DDF58006",
    "text": "Header block + §1 (motivation for replacing the single shared `unfolded` flag with per-viewer `TreeView`s) → `discussion/treeview.md` itself (rationale/motivation, matching how other design Context sections link out to a specific discussion heading rather than restating the \"why\" inline).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CE1DDF58007",
    "text": "§2 (three tiers of perata), §3 (`Profile`/`TreeView` data model), §4 (worked example), §5 (rendering: three display tiers), §6 (two paths to the same node — canonical position rule), §7 (`Profile`: lightweight identity), §8 (git separation, `.state/` vs. tracked mirror), §9 (migrating existing `unfolded` data), §12 (depth legibility marker), §13 (viewcone zoom + its own worked example and resolved cross-cone rule) → `design/treeview.md`, as the normative current-state architecture — stripped of \"corrected from an earlier draft\"/\"loosened from a narrower version\" narrative, which reads as history, not standing design (matching `design/packaging.md`'s own precedent: no \"corrected from X\" language survives into Design there either).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CE1DDF58008",
    "text": "§10 (\"Open questions — all resolved\") → mostly `history/treeview.md`, as a resolved-decision log; the one still-live crystallized behavior it describes (the `\"default\"` `Profile`/`TreeView` bootstrap) gets folded into `design/treeview.md`'s own description of that behavior directly, not left phrased as a Q&A.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CE1DDF58009",
    "text": "§13.3 (upward-pointing-link gap in viewcone zoom) and §14 (stale `TreeView.unfolds` references) → `issues/treeview.md` if still open, `history/treeview.md` if the verification pass above finds them fixed; either way the two options weighed for each fix are `discussion/treeview.md` material (rationale for the chosen direction), not `design`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF5800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CE1DDF5800A",
    "text": "§15 (bare `kg:unfold` should peek, not mutate, when `--view` is fully omitted) → same split as above, pending verification: `history/treeview.md` if landed, `issues/treeview.md` + `planning/treeview.md` if not.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
