    "title": "**Stale `TreeView.unfolds` references have no general cleanup**",
    "text": "**Stale `TreeView.unfolds` references have no general cleanup**: `TreeView.unfold(ref)` appends with no existence check, and the only cleanup — a reactive strip-on-hard-delete — only fires at the exact moment a specific id is hard-deleted; nothing revisits an *existing* `unfolds` entry against what's currently live. Confirmed live: `.state/TreeView.jsonld`'s `default` view has named 10 `BlockNode` ids with no corresponding document at all, after unrelated reconciliation churn elsewhere reassigned/removed the blocks those ids used to name. See [Settled](../discussion/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1FFSR8006) for the chosen fix direction.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CE1GW638005",
    "text": "**A bare `aperas unfold <ref>` (no `--view` flag at all) mutates the `\"default\"` view instead of peeking**: should be read-only — resolve and print a preview, touching no `TreeView` state — matching `aperas tree`'s own no-view default. Today it falls into the same bootstrap-and-mutate path that `aperas unfold <ref> --view` (flag present, no name) is supposed to trigger. `aperas fold`'s own no-`--view` case isn't resolved by this — folding presupposes some view's state to collapse, so a peek-equivalent doesn't obviously apply.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638006:links:Link:00CF10KBB8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CEDP10P8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638006:links:Link:00CF10KBB8000:props:StringProp:00CF10KBB8001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "725"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**No raw single-node inspection command**",
    "text": "**No raw single-node inspection command**: `aperas tree`/`aperas backlinks --text` only ever show a rendered preview (title + truncated, anchor-stripped abstract) — right for browsing, not for verifying a stored field is exactly what's about to be pushed back via `aperas update`/`aperas insert`, or for reading a field no command shows at all (`props`, `tombstonedAt`). `aperas project --dry-run` reconstructs real markdown but only at the whole-artifact level. Today the only way to see a node's exact stored state is a direct `BlockNode.jsonld`/`ArtifactNode.jsonld` read outside the CLI entirely. Originally tracked under packaging, relocated here since it's a node-inspection gap, not a packaging one — the same gap the [`aperas` skill's own item 8](../history/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEDP10P8001) independently names — that gap's skill-script stage; `aperas show <ref>` below is the still-open toolset-update stage of the same lifecycle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638007",
