    "title": "**GFM task-list items round-trip broken**",
    "text": "**GFM task-list items round-trip broken**: originally found here: [archive-migration discussion](../discussion/archive-migration.md#id/BlockNode:00CE0HD0HG007) — `- [ ] text` reportedly stored the literal `[ ] ` marker inside the block's own `.text` alongside a separate `checked: false` prop, so `aperas project` would re-emit `- [ ] ` on top of the leftover `[ ] `, doubling to `- [ ] [ ] text`. Re-tested live during the list-consumption migration (both a direct `parseMarkdownTree`/`serializeBlock` round trip and a real `aperas insert` against the live corpus): does not reproduce, renders correctly. `git log` shows the checkbox-handling code in `astParser.ts` has never changed since it was first written. No corroborating evidence anywhere in the graph that this was ever actually observed broken in a real projected artifact — awaiting a decision on whether to close as not-reproducible or keep open pending further investigation. See [list-consumption discussion](../discussion/list-consumption.md#id/BlockNode:00CE8J339R001) for the re-test note.",
