    "title": "00CE1GW638008",
    "text": "**`List` isn't consumed by a preceding `Heading` the way a single paragraph already is**: resolved by [list-consumption](../design/list-consumption.md#id/BlockNode:00CE32GQM8001) — a heading whose only content is a list (no leading paragraph to consume) now dissolves the list's items as the heading's own flat children (case 3 of the unified law) instead of leaving them wrapped in a separate `list`-typed node. Not literally merged into `.text` the way a lone paragraph is (a list can't collapse into a scalar string), but no longer floats as a separate, opaque child block either — see [History](../history/list-consumption.md#id/BlockNode:00CE32GW3G002). Originally found here: [archive-migration discussion](../discussion/archive-migration.md#id/BlockNode:00CE0HD0HG007).",
