    "title": "Verified live, via direct reads of `astParser.ts`/`project.ts`",
    "text": "Verified live, via direct reads of `astParser.ts`/`project.ts`: consumption (a list adopts into whichever real node immediately precedes it) and self-dissolution (a list adopts into its own container once that container's leading paragraph has been consumed into its `.text`) were already correctly implemented — including the specific safeguard against two adjacent lists corrupting each other's props (`adoptionAnchor` resets after every list, adopted or orphaned). No code change needed for either case; this design's contribution is stating them as one law and identifying the one case they don't yet cover.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE32GW3G003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
