        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CE5EHVXR008:links:Link:00CE6C6RWG000:props:StringProp:00CE6C6RWG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "138"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Inserting a list item always spawns a fresh run-leader**",
    "text": "**Inserting a list item always spawns a fresh run-leader**: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CE5EHVXR008' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> see [Open Issues](../issues/list-consumption.md#id/BlockNode:00CE32GRZG002) — live-tested while writing this same Resolved section. A freshly `aperas insert`-ed bullet always parses as its own orphaned one-item list, so it gets its own explicit `orderedList`/`startIndex` per the normalization rule — marking it a run-leader relative to whatever precedes it, even an ordinary continuation of the identical list. Renders with a spurious blank line before it; not corruption (bullet type and numbering stay correct), but a real regression from the old anchor-owns-it model, where a freshly inserted item carried no prop of its own. No fix designed yet. Confirmed live twice more since: pushing a list's full corrected content instead of a bare `--after` insert avoids it, since the new item joins the same parsed run as a continuation rather than becoming its own orphaned list.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE32GXH000D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
