    "title": "**`aperas unfold`'s raw preview omits the tombstone tag `aperas tree --view` shows**",
    "text": "**`aperas unfold`'s raw preview omits the tombstone tag `aperas tree --view` shows**: found live while investigating a cross-linking question in `list-consumption` — `aperas unfold BlockNode:00CE1GW638002 --view <name>` printed two children (00CE5QD6W8001, 00CE1GW638003) with no marker distinguishing them from live siblings, read as stray/anomalous at first. Re-running `aperas tree BlockNode:00CE1GW638002 --view <name>` on the identical, already-unfolded subtree appended a plain `(tombstoned)` suffix to those same two lines — confirming both commands know the node is tombstoned, but only `tree` surfaces it. **Proposed fix — don't just add the tag to `unfold`; hide tombstoned nodes from default output entirely, in both commands**, revealed only via an explicit `--tombstoned` flag. A tombstoned node is dead data retained solely for id-stability; showing it unmarked in a raw exploratory listing invites exactly the misreading that happened here. See [Issues](../issues/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE8T6W7G001) for the tracked gap.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58003",
