        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CE8XWZK0004",
    "text": "Investigating a graph question (a cross-doc linking gap) was done entirely via `grep`/`find`/`Read` on projected `.md` files and a raw `BlockNode.jsonld` read, never via `aperas backlinks`/`unfold` — while the findings report itself cited the skill's own item 18 (\"work the graph, not a folder of files\"). Redone correctly afterward with `aperas backlinks`/`unfold`, which reproduced the same conclusions in far fewer steps. The gap: item 18 states the principle but doesn't make it a hard habit-check — nothing in the skill prompts \"before grepping, ask whether an `aperas` verb already does this.\"",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0005:links:Link:00CE8XX0M8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CE8T49MR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0005:links:Link:00CE8XX0M8000:props:StringProp:00CE8XX0M8001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "250"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0005:links:Link:00CE8XX0M8002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CE8T6W7G001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0005:links:Link:00CE8XX0M8002:props:StringProp:00CE8XX0M8003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "321"
          }
