    ],
    "title": "## Open Issues",
    "text": "None — all six are resolved by the v1 restructure, see Resolved below. New gaps found while working the graph are parked in [Freeflow](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001) until a dedicated home exists.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G003:links:Link:00CEA6RHSR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG003",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G003:links:Link:00CEA6RHSR000:props:StringProp:00CEA6RHSR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "452"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G003:props:StringProp:00CEA5KXDR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G003:props:StringProp:00CEA5KXE0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The document is flat where the subject matter is layered**",
    "text": "**The document is flat where the subject matter is layered**: all eighteen items sit at one rank, so a statement the whole skill depends on (\"work the graph, not a folder of files\") is typographically indistinguishable from a shell-quoting gotcha. A reader has no way to tell which items explain the others and which are implementation detail, and no basis for deciding what to re-read when something goes wrong. The target shape is the four levels in [Architecture](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG003). **Resolved**: four levels now, Philosophy through Mechanics.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The load-bearing statement is last**",
    "text": "**The load-bearing statement is last**: the graph-substance principle is item 18, reached only after seventeen mechanical rules that are themselves consequences of it. A reader who stops early gets the consequences without the cause — exactly the failure mode that produced the grep-instead-of-traverse incident, where the rule was cited correctly in a report while being violated in the same breath. **Resolved**: the graph-substance principle is promoted to Orientation, ahead of every mechanical rule that follows from it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Settled facts and live cautions are not distinguished**",
    "text": "**Settled facts and live cautions are not distinguished**: item 13's create-and-promote dance describes a failure mode a completed migration has since removed, but nothing at the item says so, so a reader keeps paying a cost whose cause is gone. There is no marking that separates \"confirmed safe now\" from \"still open\" from \"never reproduced\". **Resolved**: every item is marked `[current]`, `[superseded]` or `[unverified]` where it stands.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The two section headings don't carve at a real joint**",
    "text": "**The two section headings don't carve at a real joint**: \"Editing discipline\" (items 1-8) and \"Working practices\" (items 9-18) split what is actually a mix — wikilink syntax and anchor placement are mechanics, staging and write-discussion-first are discipline, and the graph-substance principle is neither. The boundary reflects the order things were learned, not any distinction a reader can use. **Resolved**: both headings are gone, replaced by the level split.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Rule and origin are inconsistently ordered within items**",
    "text": "**Rule and origin are inconsistently ordered within items**: some items lead with the rule and attach the incident; others open with narrative and leave the rule to be inferred. The incident must travel with the rule — a rule whose \"why\" is lost gets misapplied at its edges — but it should not have to be excavated. **Resolved**: items are stated rule-first, with the incident attached rather than leading.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**No stated scope boundary**",
    "text": "**No stated scope boundary**: nothing says what belongs in this skill versus `kg-doc-ingest`, versus a concern doc in the graph, versus a tool-gap issue. Tool gaps discovered in practice have accumulated inline as prose caveats (items 8, 17) rather than being tracked where they can be closed. **Resolved**: stated in the skill — this skill owns working the graph, `kg-doc-ingest` owns getting existing text into it, and project facts live in concern docs the skill only points at.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
