  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Aperas Skill — Planning",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CEA5M69R000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8002",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Implementation Plan",
    "text": "Restructure in place rather than rewriting from a blank file. Every existing item was paid for by a live incident, so the content is the asset and the arrangement is the defect — a fresh draft would silently drop hard-won specifics that no one would notice missing until the incident recurred.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8003",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEA5M6S8003",
    "text": "The verbatim copy already dumped into the discussion doc is the working surface for the rewrite: each item is an addressable block, so the reorganisation can be discussed and tracked by citing blocks rather than line numbers in a file that is about to move.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8004:links:Link:00CEA6RAGR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG003",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8004:links:Link:00CEA6RAGR000:props:StringProp:00CEA6RAGR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "114"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CEA5M6S8004",
    "text": "Order matters. The level assignment comes first and everything else follows from it, because an item's level (see [Architecture](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG003)) determines both where it lands and how it gets reworded — the same fact stated as philosophy and as mechanics is not the same sentence.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Task Breakdown",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8006",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8007",
