      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800C",
      "BlockNode:00CEB17CPG009",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFKN30008",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFKN30009",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFKN3000A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8006:props:StringProp:00CEA5M7QR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8006:props:StringProp:00CEA5M7QR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CEDFKN30000",
    "text": "Assign every one of the eighteen existing items to a level — philosophy, orientation, discipline, or mechanics — by asking what explains it, not where it was first noticed. Items that split across levels get split.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEDFKN30001",
    "text": "Restate the philosophy and orientation levels from the settled framing, so they read as the cause of what follows rather than as two more rules.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEDFKN30002",
    "text": "Rewrite each remaining item rule-first, with its originating incident attached rather than leading.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Mark every item's status explicitly where it stands",
    "text": "Mark every item's status explicitly where it stands: confirmed-current, superseded by a landed change, or unverified.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEDFKN30004",
    "text": "Harvest an example for each level in the kind that level takes — a contrast pair for philosophy, a traversal transcript for orientation, one full worked loop for discipline, a command plus its exact failure text for mechanics. Draw every one from a real recorded incident; synthesise nothing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEDFKN30005",
    "text": "Extract accumulated tool gaps out of the prose into tracked issues in the graph, leaving the skill with a pointer rather than a growing caveat list.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEDFKN30006",
    "text": "Decide the scope boundary against `kg-doc-ingest` and against concern docs, and state it in the skill itself.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Verification Plan",
    "text": "The rewrite succeeds if an agent reading only the first two levels behaves correctly in the ordinary case — graph-first, traversal-first — without having reached any mechanics.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800E",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY0001",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY0002",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY0003",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY0004",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY8000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEA5M6S800E",
    "text": "Two concrete checks, both available from this corpus rather than from judgement alone. First, every incident already recorded in this concern's discussion should be predictable from a statement at the philosophy or discipline level; one that isn't marks a gap at that level, not a missing gotcha. Second, the grep-instead-of-traverse failure specifically should be prevented by something a reader meets before any CLI verb appears, since that failure happened to a reader who had the rule available and still did not apply it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Aperas Skill — History",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CEA5MGZR000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8002",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Current Status",
    "text": "The restructure has landed. `skills/aperas/SKILL.md` (reached by symlink from `.agents/skills/` and `.claude/skills/`) is now v1: four levels — Philosophy, Orientation, Discipline, Mechanics — read top-down, each item marked `[current]`, `[superseded]` or `[unverified]`, with a scope statement and a worked example at each of the first three levels.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8003:links:Link:00CECFCSKR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8003:links:Link:00CECFCSKR000:props:StringProp:00CECFCSKR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "521"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CEA5MHD8003",
    "text": "All eighteen original items survived, relevelled rather than rewritten — item 18's graph-substance principle promoted to Orientation where it explains the rest, items 1/2/11/12/17 and half of 14 gathered into Discipline around an explicit edit loop, and the syntax and command-level items collected into Mechanics. Item 14's other half (the Freeflow document shape) left the skill entirely for `design/documentation.md`, and item 8's tool gap became a pointer to its tracked issue instead of inline prose. Remaining from [Task Breakdown](../planning/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005): step 5's example harvest is partially done — the contrast pair, the traversal transcript and the edit loop are in, the Mechanics command-plus-failure-text examples are not yet systematic.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Milestones",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8005",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8006",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8007",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8008",
      "BlockNode:00CEDP10P8001",
      "BlockNode:00CEFF85V8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8005:props:StringProp:00CEA5MJBR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8005:props:StringProp:00CEA5MJBR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CEA5MHD8005",
    "text": "The skill was factored out of `kg-doc-ingest` once a second workflow needed the same practices, and grew from there by accretion — one item per live incident, appended in the order things were learned.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEA5MHD8006",
    "text": "Its full text was dumped verbatim into this concern's discussion doc, split so that every item is an individually addressable block, making the rewrite discussable by citation rather than by line number.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The governing philosophy was stated explicitly for the first time",
    "text": "The governing philosophy was restated in the graph itself for the first time — the ApeironNgn-era corpus had been operating on it without ever naming it, which is why the skill's most load-bearing statement had ended up last in a flat list. It is not new: `archive/Aperas-design.md` has carried it from the start, as the Apeiron/Aperas/Peras triad, the fluid-core-versus-crystallized-interface split, and deep read/deep write as the Multi-Agent Projection Pattern's defining capabilities. That founding document is itself written as an unbounded tree of nested list items with no headings at all — practising the Freeflow shape the skill only later stated as a rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEA5MHD8008",
    "text": "A gap between documented practice and normative design was found and closed in the same pass: the Freeflow-as-unbounded-tree rule existed only in the skill, never in `design/documentation.md`'s own Scratchpad section, which still showed a heading-based example. Folded back into the design doc.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
