    "title": "00CEFF85V8001",
    "text": "**The rewrite's own eval set was run for the first time, and it caught a real bug**: four prompts ([discussion](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEDVTB68001)), each graded by direct graph inspection — never the acting subagent's own report — across two arms, v0 (extracted from git history) and the current v1 skill. Three of four prompts passed cleanly on both arms. The fourth, `complete-list-push`, exposed [a real, previously-undocumented reconcile bug](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEF7TB2G000): `aperas update <heading-id>` matches piped list content against the stored children array by raw position, tombstones included, not by content/key as both skill versions claim. v0's own prescribed technique (push the complete reconstructed list to the parent heading) triggers it; v1's updated Mechanics guidance (prefer `insert --after` for unordered lists) happens to avoid it. Confirms the restructure is measurably safer in at least one concrete case, not merely better organized.",
