    "title": "**Dense cross-linking pass planned**",
    "text": "**Dense cross-linking pass planned**: unfolded aperas-skill.md and archive-migration.md's full concern-doc-sets together into a `dense-link` view to check for real, un-linked relationships between them. Plan: (1) direct-link the \"aperas\" skill mention in [Implementation Plan](../planning/archive-migration.md#id/BlockNode:00CE01Y1Z8002) to [aperas-skill's Growth section](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG00E), since \"fold anything learned back\" is exactly that section's bottom-up-emergence practice; (2) add an indirect-edge node here noting `archive/Aperas-design.md` is simultaneously this migration's least-structured pending sub-task ([Open Questions](../discussion/archive-migration.md#id/BlockNode:00CE0HD0H8001)) and aperas-skill's already-load-bearing philosophy source ([Architecture](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG004), [History](../history/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8007)); (3) add a Settled entry here cross-linking this design doc's disk-first/graph-first [Architecture](../design/archive-migration.md#id/BlockNode:00CE01XZPG008) split to aperas-skill's own [scope-boundary Settled entry](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CE8XWZK000B); (4) link the completed treeview sub-task [milestone](../history/archive-migration.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1JRAC0004) to aperas-skill's Discipline-level [worked-loop example](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEB8N5EG001), as a live instance of that principle. All four executed and verified via `aperas backlinks`.",
