    "title": "00CF060R78001",
    "text": "**`archive/Aperas-design.md` is simultaneously this sub-task's least-structured pending item and already-load-bearing philosophy elsewhere**: the open question above is only about how to eventually split it into a concern-doc-set — it says nothing about the fact that, still unmigrated, it's already cited as founding source in [aperas-skill's own Architecture](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG004) (the Multi-Agent Projection Pattern, deep read/deep write as its defining capabilities) and in [aperas-skill's History](../history/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8007) (the Apeiron/Aperas/Peras triad, restated in the graph itself for the first time). Whatever structure this eventual brainstorm lands on should account for citations that already exist against the unmigrated file, not just its own content.",
