  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF10ATY800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Not pursued",
    "text": "Not pursued: the `packaging`↔`archive-migration` rename-collision lead needs more checking before acting; flagging rather than guessing. Also noting, not fixing: `history/linking.md` already links down into `discussion/linking.md` in several places — pre-existing practice that appears to violate the stated citation-direction rule; out of scope to correct retroactively here, but worth knowing about when applying the rule strictly going forward. All ten links executed and verified via `aperas backlinks`; the two indirect edges landed as new nodes in `discussion/linking.md` and `discussion/list-consumption.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF10ATY8000",
