  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Verification Plan",
    "text": "Each Group A fix is checked against its own already-documented repro, not just a fresh test written for the occasion — item 1 against the exact `issues/treeview.md` list shape that exposed it, item 2 against `list-consumption`'s eval sandbox. Item 6's fix is checked by forcing the failure directly: fail a later file mid-batch `kg:ingest` and confirm earlier files' writes didn't commit (the matching single-`kg:insert` check now lives in `cli`'s own planning doc). A fix isn't done until its Open Issues entry can honestly move to Resolved with the actual mechanism named, matching this concern's own citation-direction discipline against guessing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
