    ],
    "title": "**Split planned: `cli` → `core` (rename) + a new, thin `cli`**",
    "text": "**Split planned: `cli` → `core` (rename) + a new, thin `cli`**: realized while scoping this batch that `packages/` is `core`/`cli`/`web` — core is the shared ApeironNgn engine, cli is a thin dispatcher over it, and web will eventually be another thin wrapper over the same core. Almost everything filed under this concern so far (items 1-4, 6, 7; the `treeview`/`linking`/`list-consumption`/`crud` Sub-Parts) is core engine content, not CLI-dispatcher content — only item 5 (`kg:insert`'s own call-ordering) and `packaging` are genuinely cli-specific. Plan: retitle and reword this doc set's own content while still at the `cli.md` paths, `git mv` all three to `core.md`, `aperas ingest --track` scoped to confirm identity survives, then move (not copy) item 5 into a freshly-created thin `cli.md`/`discussion/cli.md`/`planning/cli.md` — `packaging` stays where it already lives, just re-indexed under the new thin `cli`'s own Sub-Parts. `documentation` and `archive-migration` are meta/process concerns about the graph itself, not part of the core/cli/webapp product split, and aren't reassigned to either. Executing next.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZE18004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
