      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CF2AEAX0003:props:StringProp:00CF2AEC10001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**A single `kg:insert` call isn't transactional**",
    "text": "**A single `kg:insert` call isn't transactional**: `kgInsert.ts`'s create mode resolves the parent, parses piped markdown into fresh nodes, checks name collisions, writes every new node into the store via `hydrateFromParsed`, resolves links, and only *then* resolves the `--after`/`--before` anchor — so an anchor-resolution failure leaves the newly-hydrated nodes live in memory, attached to nothing, with no rollback. `rejectSlugPathCollisions` is deliberately ordered ahead of hydration; this is a missing second guard (resolve/validate the anchor beside that same check, before any hydration), not a structural problem. `aperas reload -- --discard` is the only current recovery. The fix is entirely within `kgInsert.ts`'s own call ordering — no `core` change needed, which is why this stays in `cli` rather than moving with its siblings.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF2AEAX0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
