    "title": "**`aperas resolve`'s title-ambiguity check doesn't filter tombstoned candidates either**",
    "text": "**`aperas resolve`'s title-ambiguity check doesn't filter tombstoned candidates either**: found live while resolving the new thin `cli.md` docs — `resolve issues/cli.md` failed with \"'cli.md' is ambiguous among: ArtifactNode:00CF2AEA78000 (\"cli.md\"), ArtifactNode:00CF1TZQV8000 (\"cli.md\")\", even though the second id was a tombstoned holder chain removed earlier in this same session. Same shape as [the dead-container gap](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG006) and the other tombstone-blind-spot findings in this batch — another site that treats a tombstoned node as if it still competes for a name. Not filed as its own Open Issue yet; parked here since it's minor and workaroundable (full-id lookup instead of bare-path resolve).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZE18004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  }
